13. Summary

The combination of "brain plus technology plus brand" barriers, which is the top player in China’s Quantified Private Enterprise, makes it difficult to be overtaken in the short term. It is in a structurally contradictory race: bound to limit size (strategic capacity bottlenecks), alpha to decline (more participants plus market efficiency), and to tighten regulation.

** AI’s influence on Queen 9 is the "two-edged sword"**: short-term enhancements (arithmetic plus data plus talent advantage benefits the head more), but there is a real threat in the medium- and long-term of strategic convergence of systemic risks and the creation of asymmetric advantages by the illusion/DeepSeek. The AI input from the three laboratories in Queen 9 needs to be translated into a verifiable performance advantage as soon as possible, otherwise the question of "AI’s marginal achievement" will grow stronger.

The essence of investing in Queen 9 is not a gamble that "it will change big" (the size is the enemy of performance), but that "it will live a cycle more than its peers in the retreat of industrial dividends." Under the current information conditions (the 2021 financing valuation may be bubbles, the alpha decline is clear, and the exit path is narrow), it is recommended** to wait for the valuation to return to reasonable intervals**.

